NUM-24: count the right end wall of a transect like the left one

buildTables()'s getFlow closed the last sub-section at the last real station
(k == Nsta - 1). For a transect the vertical end wall added after it has no
area, so its flow is zero and its wetted perimeter was dropped, while the left
end wall is carried into the first sub-section. Close a transect's last
sub-section at the wall slice instead (k == Nsta when add_end_walls), so both
end walls count, as the reference manual's algorithm prescribes. Streets keep
Nsta - 1, so their results do not change.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-24_swmm600.patch

